STTILECFG: decode at VEX.W0, not VEX.W1

STTILECFG is VEX.128.66.0F38.W0 49 !(11):000:bbb (SDM Vol. 2, and what
every assembler emits — LLVM/GNU as encode W0). The VEX 0F38 49 opcode group
bound BX_IA_STTILECFG to ATTR_VEX_W1, so the real instruction never matched
and raised #UD unconditionally, while LDTILECFG/TILERELEASE/TILEZERO in the
same group correctly asked for W0.

Found by this crate's differential suite the day AMX was first compiled into
the vendored core (BX_SUPPORT_AMX had been 0); see docs/backend-differences.md
§4k. Still present on upstream master as of 2026-09-12.

The hunk below is deliberately comment-free, so that this file can be sent
upstream as-is.

--- a/cpu/decoder/fetchdecode_opmap_avx.cc
+++ b/cpu/decoder/fetchdecode_opmap_avx.cc
@@ -1003,7 +1003,7 @@ static const Bit64u BxOpcodeGroup_VEX_0F3847[] = {
 static const Bit64u BxOpcodeGroup_VEX_0F3849[] = {
   form_opcode(ATTR_SSE_NO_PREFIX | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_VL128 | ATTR_NNN0 | ATTR_RRR0 | ATTR_MODC0 | ATTR_IS64, BX_IA_TILERELEASE),
   form_opcode(ATTR_SSE_NO_PREFIX | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_VL128 | ATTR_MOD_MEM | ATTR_IS64, BX_IA_LDTILECFG),
-  form_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_66 | ATTR_VEX_W1 | ATTR_VL128 | ATTR_MOD_MEM | ATTR_IS64, BX_IA_STTILECFG),
+  form_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_66 | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_VL128 | ATTR_MOD_MEM | ATTR_IS64, BX_IA_STTILECFG),
   last_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_F2 | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_VL128 | ATTR_RRR0 | ATTR_MODC0 | ATTR_IS64, BX_IA_TILEZERO_Tnnn)
 };

